  <!--
    1.12.229 -> 1.12.230, UNIT 292 TASK 1, UNDER HM-DEC-150. A PATCH, AND IT CHANGES NO BEHAVIOUR AT
    ALL - IT MEASURES ONE.

      Step 4's trace ran before anything was threaded, and it needed a measurement rather than a
      reading: PressingFt4TunesAndDecodesFt4Tests drives thirty seconds of band carrying four real
      FT4 transmissions through MainWindowViewModel.ShowDecodes with FT4 chosen, and records what
      the tab does with it today. Two whole FIFTEEN-second slots cut, read by Ft8Sharp.Deep, and
      nought of the four messages back. That is the button that tunes correctly and then decodes
      nothing for the rest of the evening, held as a fact rather than described as one.

      The test is rewritten by tasks 2 and 3 to assert the right answers. Nothing in src/ changed.

    No file under src/Ft8Sharp/ changed.
