      MFSK is the ADIF mode FT4, JS8, MSK144 and half a dozen others share, so both ledger surfaces
      showed three different modes under one word. The log window's mode cell now reads MFSK dot FT4
      where the record carries a submode, and the Log dialog gains a Submode row carrying SUBMODE
      beside the mode row's MODE.

      **ABSENT IS ABSENT, AND THAT IS THE HALF THAT COULD HAVE GONE QUIETLY WRONG.** An FT8
      contact's submode is not unrecorded - it does not exist, and unit 291 proved the record
      carries no SUBMODE tag at all. So there is no cell reading `not recorded` on every FT8 row in
      a table whose other absences are real, and no dialog row reading `Hamlet did not hear this`
      about a field it heard everything of. An FT8 contact's cell is byte-identical and its dialog
      still says `Hamlet heard all 11 of these`.

      Both surfaces or neither: a window that shows it beside a dialog that does not teaches the
      operator to trust one screen and not the other. 4 new, 36 of 36 inherited ledger tests green.

