  <!--
    1.12.253 -> 1.12.254, UNIT 296 TASK 3, UNDER HM-DEC-150. A PATCH, AND AGAIN THE PRODUCT IS A
    MEASUREMENT: no file under src/ changed. A denser FT4 analysis grid costs zero lines of source
    to try, so four were tried on task 1b's own lattice. The answer is one axis and not the other.
    Frequency oversampling above 2 destroys the decode and destroys the ON-GRID one first - 2x4 and
    4x4 both fall from 36 of 36 to 0 of 36 at -13 dB - because Ft8Monitor's analysis frame is
    BlockSize x FrequencyOversampling samples long, so at 4 it spans four FT4 symbols and a 4-FSK
    tone that changes every symbol is smeared across the window. Time oversampling costs nothing of
    the kind: at 4x2 the placement average at -13 dB goes 808 of 900 to 894 of 900 and the worst
    cell 19 of 36 to 34 of 36, the on-grid cell does not move, and one slot costs 151 ms against a
